      "title": "Simplifying Expressions in Radians Using the Sum and Difference Formulas"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "9905b87b-56db-5ed7-9b69-092ae584e18f",
      ":question/problem": "Express $\\cos\\left(x+\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)$ in terms of $\\sin x$ or $\\cos x$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Use the sum formula:\n\n$$\n\\cos(u+v)=\\cos u\\cos v-\\sin u\\sin v\n$$\n\nWith $u=x$ and $v=\\frac{\\pi}{2}$, the exact values are $\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)=0$ and $\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)=1$. Substitute and collect the terms in the requested order:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos\\left(x+\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)&=\\cos x\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)-\\sin x\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)\\\\\n&=\\cos x\\cdot\\left(0\\right)-\\sin x\\cdot\\left(1\\right)\\\\\n&=-\\sin x.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "f3a11a7f-99f1-5aef-8809-c37fee57bc43",
