    "question": {
      ":question/id": "6078c992-7dd1-5b2d-9ff6-aacc7a58c2aa",
      ":question/problem": "Express $\\cos\\left(x-\\frac{3\\pi}{2}\\right)$ in terms of $\\sin x$ or $\\cos x$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Use the difference formula:\n\n$$\n\\cos(u-v)=\\cos u\\cos v+\\sin u\\sin v\n$$\n\nWith $u=x$ and $v=\\frac{3\\pi}{2}$, the exact values are $\\cos\\left(\\frac{3\\pi}{2}\\right)=0$ and $\\sin\\left(\\frac{3\\pi}{2}\\right)=-1$. Substitute and collect the terms in the requested order:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos\\left(x-\\frac{3\\pi}{2}\\right)&=\\cos x\\cos\\left(\\frac{3\\pi}{2}\\right)+\\sin x\\sin\\left(\\frac{3\\pi}{2}\\right)\\\\\n&=\\cos x\\cdot\\left(0\\right)+\\sin x\\cdot\\left(-1\\right)\\\\\n&=-\\sin x.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
